  "generated_text": "To solve for \\( g(4) \\), we need to determine the function \\( g(x) \\) first. We know that \\( f(x) = 2x - 3 \\) and \\( g(f(x)) = 5 - 4x \\). We need to express \\( g \\) in terms of \\( x \\).\n\nLet's denote \\( y = f(x) \\). Then \\( y = 2x - 3 \\). We need to express \\( x \\) in terms of \\( y \\). Solving for \\( x \\) in the equation \\( y = 2x - 3 \\):\n\n\\[\ny = 2x - 3 \\implies y + 3 = 2x \\implies x = \\frac{y + 3}{2}\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute \\( x = \\frac{y + 3}{2} \\) into the expression for \\( g(f(x)) \\):\n\n\\[\ng(f(x)) = g(y) = 5 - 4x = 5 - 4 \\left( \\frac{y + 3}{2} \\right) = 5 - 2(y + 3) = 5 - 2y - 6 = -2y - 1\n\\]\n\nSo, the function \\( g(x) \\) is:\n\n\\[\ng(x) = -2x - 1\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find \\( g(4) \\):\n\n\\[\ng(4) = -2(4) - 1 = -8 - 1 = -9\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-9}\n\\]",
